Subject: [PATCH] wave: preserve reassociation after completed key retirement

The native SME can retire the old association and its group keys, then prepare
the target BSS in the same wiphy transaction. Acknowledged group-key revocation
removes the firmware VAP. Queuing another terminal stop after the old peer and
association are already gone prevents the target BSSID callback from reopening
that VAP; the queued work cannot clear the barrier until reassociation returns.

Avoid that redundant stop request only for successful VAP removal after the
native peer and association have both retired. Keep the stopped/uninitialized
state for the existing acknowledged activation and BSS setup path. Do not clear
an existing pending stop or relax failed-revocation and live-peer handling.

--- a/wireless/driver/linux/mac80211.c
+++ b/wireless/driver/linux/mac80211.c
@@ -1798,8 +1798,18 @@
         wv_iface_inf->vap_stopped = true;
         wv_iface_inf->is_initialized = FALSE;
       }
-      wv_iface_inf->stop_pending = true;
-      wiphy_work_queue(hw->wiphy, &wv_iface_inf->stop_work);
+      /* Direct reassociation can prepare the next BSSID before queued
+       * wiphy work runs. An acknowledged VAP removal after the old native
+       * peer and association retired needs no further terminal stop.
+       * Keep stopped/uninitialized and any earlier fault barrier; the
+       * next BSSID still owns checked activation and BSS initialization.
+       */
+      if (ret != MTLK_ERR_OK || removed != WAVE_KEY_VAP_REMOVED ||
+          vif->cfg.assoc ||
+          wv_iface_inf->current_state != IEEE80211_STA_NOTEXIST) {
+        wv_iface_inf->stop_pending = true;
+        wiphy_work_queue(hw->wiphy, &wv_iface_inf->stop_work);
+      }
     }
     break;
   }
